The Basics:

The VP of Solutions Architecture - ServiceNow leads a team of Solution Architects within the Sales Alliances organization, overseeing the design and delivery of integrated Tanium and ServiceNow solutions throughout the full sales lifecycle. This individual brings senior-level&nbsp; expertise &nbsp;in ServiceNow consulting engagements and serves as a thought leader in go-to-market strategy and solutions development. The role requires strong executive presence, cross-functional collaboration, and a proven ability to alig n technical architecture with strategic business outcomes. &nbsp;

What you’ll do:

• Lead and develop a team of Solution Architects, providing performance management, time allocation guidance, and process efficiency recommendations to drive team excellence &nbsp;

• Define field strategy priorities and align with sales, product, and delivery stakeholders to accelerate pipeline and revenue growth &nbsp;

• Engage C-level and executive stakeholders to position integrated Tanium and ServiceNow solutions and align technical capabilities with customer priorities &nbsp;

• Architect scalable, secure, and resilient solutions&nbsp;leveraging&nbsp;deep&nbsp;expertise&nbsp;across ServiceNow modules (ITSM, ITOM, SecOps, GRC, Discovery, CMDB,&nbsp;IntegrationHub) and the Tanium platform (Asset, Patch, Comply, Threat Response, Deploy) &nbsp;

• Lead technical discovery sessions, architecture reviews, and gap analyses to develop reference architectures and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;a current solution documentation library &nbsp;

• Design and deliver prototypes, proof-of-concept engagements, and tailored demonstrations to&nbsp;validate&nbsp;solutions and accelerate customer decision-making &nbsp;

• Build compelling business cases in partnership with the Value Engineering team, including ROI and TCO models and competitive assessments, to support strategic sales initiatives &nbsp;

• Enable and coach sales teams on solution selling methodologies, and&nbsp;monitor&nbsp;post-sale adoption and expansion opportunities to drive customer success &nbsp;

• Report internal KPIs to leadership and external KPIs to customers, ensuring transparency and accountability across the solution architecture function &nbsp;

• Guide the development of go-to-market materials&nbsp;leveraging&nbsp;AI tools and emerging technologies to support scalable, repeatable solution offerings &nbsp;

We’re looking for someone with:

• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science , Information Technology, Business, or a related field, or equivalent experience
&nbsp;

• 5-8 years of experience in solutions architecture, pre-sales engineering, or technical consulting, with a focus on ServiceNow and/or endpoint management platforms &nbsp;

• Demonstrated experience leading or managing a team of technical professionals in a fast-paced, sales-aligned environment &nbsp;

• Proven&nbsp; track record &nbsp;conducting ServiceNow consulting engagements across modules such as ITSM, ITOM, SecOps, GRC, Discovery, CMDB, and&nbsp; IntegrationHub &nbsp;

• Experience integrating Tanium and ServiceNow with Microsoft ecosystems using REST APIs, webhooks, and middleware solutions &nbsp;

• Experience developing and presenting ROI/TCO models, competitive positioning materials, and executive-level proposals
&nbsp;

• Proficiency &nbsp;with ServiceNow platform modules including ITSM, ITOM, SecOps, GRC, Discovery, CMDB, and&nbsp; IntegrationHub &nbsp;

• Proficiency &nbsp;with Tanium platform capabilities including Asset, Patch, Comply, Threat Response, and Deploy &nbsp;

• Strong architectural skills including CMDB modeling, security architecture design, and performance tuning &nbsp;

• Familiarity with integration technologies including REST APIs, webhooks, and middleware platforms &nbsp;

• Experience with value selling methodologies and customer journey development across the sales cycle &nbsp;

• Proficiency &nbsp;using AI-based tools for the development of go-to-market materials

